BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-w
 ebsite.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-website.jpg
UID:TjYABAnpcKQ1xJyl93ALF
SUMMARY:Inprint Cool Brains! Series presents Elizabeth Acevedo
DTSTAMP:20260720T055737Z
DTSTART:20261018T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Free tickets will be available starting Monday\, September 14\,
	 2026. \n \n\nFree and open to the public\nFree copies of Anger Is Only a 
	Shadow for the first 100 families\nConversation and Q&A with Acevedo\, led
	 by Houston writer Jasminne Mendez\nMeet the author followed by a book sal
	e and signing\nBus scholarships available for student groups – full schola
	rships for public schools\, partial scholarships for private schools upon 
	availability. For information\, email info@inprint.org\n\nDiscounted books
	 available through Kindred Stories\n\n\nAnd more!\n\n\nThe 2026/2027 Inpri
	nt Cool Brains! Series proudly presents National Book Award winner and ren
	owned poet Elizabeth Acevedo\, sharing her new YA novel Anger Is Only a Sh
	adow. \nKnown for YA novels filled with poetry\, humor\, and heart\, Eliza
	beth Acevedo is the New York Times-bestselling author of The Poet X\, whic
	h won the National Book Award for Young People’s Literature\, the Michael 
	L. Printz Award\, the Pura Belpré Award\, the Carnegie medal\, the Boston 
	Globe–Horn Book Award\, and the Walter Award. She is also the author of Wi
	th the Fire on High\, which was named a best book of the year by the New Y
	ork Public Library\, NPR\, Publishers Weekly\, and School Library Journal\
	; and Clap When You Land\, which was a Boston Globe–Horn Book Honor book a
	nd a Kirkus finalist. Acevedo is a National Poetry Slam Champion and serve
	d as the 2022 Young People’s Poet Laureate. \n“An irresistible story of fa
	mily connection\, resilience\, and loyalty” (Kirkus starred review)\, Ange
	r Is Only a Shadow is Acevedo’s powerful new YA novel in prose and poetry.
	 Lil is anything but small. She’s rebellious\, she’s loyal\; she’s figurin
	g out what kind of good person she wants to be\, or if she wants to be a g
	ood person at all. But more than anything? Lil wants to be free. When her 
	instinct for freedom leads to another stay in D.C. juvenile detention\, Li
	l knows she’s lucky to just be on probation. But judgment\, guilt\, and an
	 ankle monitor weigh heavily on her\, and she can’t shake that pinned-down
	 feeling. The only person who might understand is her big brother\, Aldwin
	. Except he’s more distant now than just the hundred miles from his colleg
	e. As her court hearing ticks closer\, a question looms over Lil as the mi
	ssed phone calls and strange texts from her brother pile up: will she stay
	 put\, or put her future freedom on the line? “A striking and nuanced port
	rait of the realities of juvenile detention and mental illness” (Publisher
	’s Weekly starred review) and “intensely genuine” (The Bulletin of the Cen
	ter for Children’s Books starred review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow a white-
	knuckle journal to self-understanding and doing the right thing\, no matte
	r the cost. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-ser
	ies-presents-elizabeth-acevedo/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-el
	izabeth-acevedo/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
